index 000000000..0ffdfd86c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/news/+state-metaclass-conflict.bugfix.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+`type(rx.State)` is `reflex.vars.BaseStateMeta` again, so a state declared with its own metaclass derived from `BaseStateMeta` (`class MyState(rx.State, metaclass=MyMeta)`) no longer raises `TypeError: metaclass conflict`. The reserved-state-name validation is unchanged; it now runs from `BaseStateMeta` itself instead of from a subclass of it.
